8350d72365b67cea8799b72a8a0fb3f75b46d4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/306994 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="306994" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/94/306994/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ieace98c297d3321b063162f1c3fe318005e2eae2" commit="1ff184b68b33a835be74b4befb50b930431ce108" commit_message="UPSTREAM: iommu: Make the iova library a module  The iova library has use outside the intel-iommu driver, thus make it a module.  Signed-off-by: Sakari Ailus &lt;sakari.ailus@linux.intel.com&gt; Signed-off-by: David Woodhouse &lt;David.Woodhouse@intel.com&gt; (cherry picked from commit 15bbdec3931e617231c12b0920e497e87ec8c2c6) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot oak-rev4  Change-Id: Ieace98c297d3321b063162f1c3fe318005e2eae2 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/306995 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="306995" owner_email="djkurtz@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/95/306995/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="I72c8533496c2c5be444ba898e481ce3f703f8ccc" commit="0f4be96b6a819eafba6fb4f239a08d405311656b" commit_message="UPSTREAM: iommu: Implement common IOMMU ops for DMA mapping  Taking inspiration from the existing arch/arm code, break out some generic functions to interface the DMA-API to the IOMMU-API. This will do the bulk of the heavy lifting for IOMMU-backed dma-mapping.  Since associating an IOVA allocator with an IOMMU domain is a fairly common need, rather than introduce yet another private structure just to do this for ourselves, extend the top-level struct iommu_domain with the notion. A simple opaque cookie allows reuse by other IOMMU API users with their various different incompatible allocator types.  Signed-off-by: Robin Murphy &lt;robin.murphy@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 0db2e5d18f76a66ca945447d9f610bed0a94ca5a  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/joro/iommu core) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot oak-rev2  Change-Id: I72c8533496c2c5be444ba898e481ce3f703f8ccc Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/292307 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="292307" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/07/292307/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ice263ab098ff165d086e8bcb49850e12212b03a8" commit="eb76aaf855c8af35b36effe3e85d1d1d44e80238" commit_message="UPSTREAM: arm64: Add IOMMU dma_ops  Taking some inspiration from the arch/arm code, implement the arch-specific side of the DMA mapping ops using the new IOMMU-DMA layer.  Since there is still work to do elsewhere to make DMA configuration happen in a more appropriate order and properly support platform devices in the IOMMU core, the device setup code unfortunately starts out carrying some workarounds to ensure it works correctly in the current state of things.  Signed-off-by: Robin Murphy &lt;robin.murphy@arm.com&gt; Acked-by: Catalin Marinas &lt;catalin.marinas@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 13b8629f651164d71f4d38b821925f93ba4236c8  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/joro/iommu core) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot oak-rev2  Change-Id: Ice263ab098ff165d086e8bcb49850e12212b03a8 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/292308 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Nicolas Boichat &lt;drinkcat@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="292308" owner_email="yong.wu@mediatek.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="17" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/08/292308/17" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ia1ac1244fefb115ff382762132cc244c46f4b83d" commit="29393131f6158fe7b50761b593524adac7bef924" commit_message="UPSTREAM: arm64: Hook up IOMMU dma_ops  With iommu_dma_ops in place, hook them up to the configuration code, so IOMMU-fronted devices will get them automatically.  Acked-by: Catalin Marinas &lt;catalin.marinas@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Robin Murphy &lt;robin.murphy@arm.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Joerg Roedel &lt;jroedel@suse.de&gt; (cherry picked from commit 876945dbf6497c7539ef958fee7ade970fbbe17a  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/joro/iommu core) Signed-off-by: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt;  BUG=chrome-os-partner:40579 TEST=build and boot oak-rev2  Change-Id: Ia1ac1244fefb115ff382762132cc244c46f4b83d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/292309 Commit-Ready: Daniel Kurtz &lt;djkurtz@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: